        "width": 1200,
        "height": 675
    },
    "description": "As LLMs are adopted across industries, it has become crucial to let them interact with real-world systems and perform tasks beyond simple text generation. Two primary methods address this need: LLM Agents and Function Calling. In short, LLM Agents are modular AI systems designed for complex, multi-step reasoning with memory and planning, while Function Calling is a simpler pattern for structured interactions between LLMs and predefined external functions, tools, or APIs.\n\nThis article provides a",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://blog.promptlayer.com/llm-agents-vs-function-calling/"
}
